.\" -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
.\" klamav-py-gui(1) — English page
.\"
.\" Maintenance conventions: same as klamav-py(1).
.\" Consistency with the parser in klamav_py/gui/app.py and with the
.\" Italian page is checked by tests/test_manpage.py.
.\"
.TH KLAMAV-PY-GUI 1 "2026-09-30" "KlamAV-Py 0.1.13" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
klamav-py-gui \- KlamAV-Py graphical interface for the ClamAV daemon
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B klamav-py-gui
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-tcp
.IR host [: port ]]
.RB [ \-\-quarantine\-dir
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-\-scan\-target
.IR path ...]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B klamav-py-gui
is the KlamAV-Py graphical interface: manual and scheduled scans,
quarantine management, signature updates, and integration with the
Dolphin context menu.
Like
.BR klamav-py (1),
it talks to
.BR clamd (8)
through its native protocol.
.PP
The application keeps running in the system tray when the window is
closed.
With the start-in-tray setting, it starts without showing the window,
unless it receives paths to scan.
.PP
Only one instance per user is allowed: a second launch forwards the
.B \-\-scan\-target
paths to the running instance and exits immediately.
.PP
Detections that are reported but not moved (heuristic signatures and
mail archives, see
.BR klamav-py (1))
are listed in the Reports page
.RI ( Segnalazioni ).
After checking one, it can be deleted, only if the path is still the same
regular file that was detected, or acknowledged: later scans, including
the scheduled system scan, no longer count its content as infected.
The same page lists the acknowledgements and revokes them.
After deleting a message from a mail archive managed by Akonadi (KMail),
.B akonadictl fsck
may be needed.
Folders that cannot be read during a scan are listed and counted
separately from errors; a folder to scan that cannot be read stops the
scan.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.BR \-\-socket ,
.B \-\-tcp
and
.B \-\-quarantine\-dir
only apply while Settings has no saved value: once Settings has been
saved, its value takes precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Path to the clamd Unix socket.
Default:
.IR /run/clamav/clamd.ctl .
.TP
.BI \-\-tcp " host\fR[\fP:port\fR]\fP"
Connect to clamd via TCP instead of a Unix socket
(default port 3310).
Incompatible with
.BR \-\-socket .
See
.B SECURITY
in
.BR klamav-py (1)
before using it.
.TP
.BI \-\-quarantine\-dir " directory"
Quarantine directory.
Default:
.IR \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/quarantine .
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-target " path\fR...\fP"
Scan one or more files or directories at startup or, if the application
is already running, forward them to the running instance.
The Dolphin context menu uses it to pass the whole selection in a single
invocation.
If the selection is too large to forward, the excess items are not sent
and a warning on standard error reports how many: in that case, scan the
folder that contains them instead.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the single-instance socket.
If it is missing or invalid, the application still starts, but without
the single-instance check, and says so.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the configuration file (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \%~/.config/KlamAV-Py/KlamAV-Py.conf
Settings.
Settings from the previous version, saved under the name KlamAV, are
migrated automatically on first start.
.TP
.I \%~/.config/systemd/user/klamav-scan.service.d/50-klamav-py.conf
Drop-in generated by Settings and by the Scheduling page when the
quarantine directory or the clamd connection of the scheduled scan differ
from the defaults, or when there are excluded folders (one
.B \-\-exclude
option each); it is removed when everything is back to the defaults.
The file is recognized by its header
.RI \(lq "Generato da KlamAV-Py" \(rq
(the text written in the file is in Italian):
it must not be edited by hand, and a file with the same name without that
header is never touched.
Other drop-ins of the unit that set
.B ExecStart
(for example an
.I override.conf
created with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user edit" )
or, with TCP,
.BR PrivateNetwork ,
are reported on save and in the Scheduling page, because they make these
settings ineffective or are overridden by them.
.TP
.I \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/acknowledged.json
Register of acknowledged detections, shared with
.BR klamav-py (1).
.TP
.I \%/usr/share/applications/klamav-py.desktop
Menu entry; its name is also the application ID that Wayland and KDE use
to match the window with its icon.
.
.SH SECURITY
.SS Single instance
The single-instance socket lives in the user's runtime directory, never
in
.IR /tmp ,
and only its owner can access it; the identity of the listening process
is verified before any data is sent to it.
If the socket cannot be created, the application still starts, with a
warning: refusing to start would let whoever causes the problem block the
antivirus.
.
.SS Quarantine directory
The rules described in
.BR klamav-py (1)
apply: volatile directories are rejected, and
.BR tmpfs " and " ramfs
file systems are accepted with a warning.
.PP
The drop-in authorizes the directory as resolved at save time: if a
symbolic link is later repointed elsewhere, the sandbox does not follow
it.
Saving Settings again regenerates the drop-in.
.
.SS Signature updates
Updating does not run
.BR freshclam (1)
as root: it restarts the system unit through
.BR pkexec (1)
and
.BR systemctl (1)
with fixed arguments and a closed list of permitted units.
The binaries involved must be owned by root and not writable by group or
others; otherwise the operation is refused.
The outcome is verified by reading the database version back from clamd.
.PP
With clamd reached over TCP, restarting the local freshclam does not
always update the database clamd uses, and updating is disabled with an
explanation: always for a remote host (the database is updated where
clamd runs); for a loopback address, when the database version reported
by clamd differs from the one in the directory set by
.B DatabaseDirectory
in the local
.BR freshclam.conf (5),
or
.I /var/lib/clamav
if it is not set (for example clamd in a container).
Host names other than
.I localhost
are not resolved and count as remote.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR klamav-py (1),
.BR clamd (8),
.BR freshclam (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
